    "created_at": "2021-08-25T08:25:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-08-25T08:25:14Z",
    "body": "> Can folks think of any repercussion of auto-sourcing the completions on init?\r\n\r\nI don't think any program I know does it. Not to mention it will make the initialization slower. In other words, I don't favor this idea.\r\n\r\n> It looks like it it would be fine for bash\r\n\r\nRemember that `bash-completion` is [a separate project](https://github.com/scop/bash-completion) and not everyone has it.\r\n\r\n> but for instance the zsh completions can't be sourced without modifications and `compinit` complicates things.\r\n\r\nSomehow related to: https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/2806#issuecomment-864547912",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
